=== Text #14 ===
> [We]’ve been working hard behind the scenes to put the foundations in place for an even more successful edition of the Summit in 2017, with even more stadium owners and operators as well as a few[ new] surprises.
The Summit will launch in a few weeks and is taking place at Croke Park, Dublin on 22-23 June.
For the next edition of the Summit, we are pleased to announce that our specialist meetings; Fan Experience Forum and Premium Seat Seminar will now be fully integrated into the main Summit.
We will still cover the same great, focused content for these two meetings, but the good news for you is that you now only need to purchase one pass for access to all our sessions, speakers, tours and networking parties.
And, you only need to take 2 days out of the office now to join the debate on the future of stadiums.
We will, of course, also be hosting the prestigious TheStadiumBusiness Awards 2017 during the Summit on the evening of 22 June (location TBC).
Nominations for the Awards will open at the end of November – Take a look[ at] our 2016 Winners Brochure to see what happened in Madrid.
That’s it for now, more details to follow very soon, we can’t wait to see you all next Summer!
Get in[ touch] if you would like to get involved in the Summit next year.[][][][][][][][][][][][][]

